      "level": 2,
      "content": "CPU Budget Philosophy",
      "disclosure": {"level": "standard", "initially_visible": true}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-cpu",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "CPU budget is measured in counts, not wall-clock. Bounds are enforced by queue caps (_MAX_PER_CONNECTION_QUEUE = 64), coalesce semantics (COALESCE_KINDS = {lifecycle_event, heartbeat}), never-drop protection (NEVER_DROP_KINDS = {error, intent_result}), and drop counting (record_dropped). ProtocolTracker.snapshot() reports only count-based metrics: coalesced_count, dropped_count, max_queue_depth, no wall-clock or elapsed-time fields. Tests validate message count and byte throughput per operation, coalesce count per drain cycle, and drop enforcement at cap boundaries.",
      "disclosure": {"level": "standard"}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Deferred Seams",
      "disclosure": {"level": "standard", "initially_visible": true}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "table-deferred",
      "type": "table",
      "columns": ["Seam", "Status", "Mitigation"],
      "rows": [
        ["WebSocketStream backpressure", "Deferred", "Bounded-queue representation (MAX_PER_CONNECTION_QUEUE + drop/coalesce) provides count-based backpressure; full WebSocketStream backpressure deferred"],
        ["E2E browser tests", "Deferred", "CLI environment constraint — Playwright/headless browser not available in test environment; contract and substrate tests cover equivalent paths"],
        ["Lifecycle file rotation", "Deferred", "BridgeLifecycleTraceWriter appends to single JSONL; file rotation policy deferred"],
        ["External network budget", "Deferred", "N/A local-only bridge; no external network path through WebSocket server"]
      ],
      "disclosure": {"level": "standard"}
    },
